UID: WORK-LIFT-REPO-ARCHITECTURE-INTO-THE-CANON
TITLE: Lift the rest of the repository's architecture and contexts into the canon
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Lift the architecture and the contexts of the rest of the repository into the
canon: the repository's own design, the model runtime, the developer tools,
the continuous integration, beads. Today that knowledge lives in the
fragment system -- the path-scoped instruction fragments under dev/fragments
and the per-package docs they compose -- as prose no check can hold to the
code. Each becomes claims of the canon (requirements, decisions, mechanisms,
evidence) with the edges that let a change re-suspect what depends on it.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
